WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.169
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 8:
Tools, Machines, and Everyday Items.

2
00:00:05.249 --> 00:00:12.605
This unit is all about the tools, machines, and
everyday items we use at home, at school, and at work.

3
00:00:12.685 --> 00:00:20.843
You will learn the names of many useful objects — from a
stapler and a microwave to a telescope and a helicopter.

4
00:00:20.923 --> 00:00:28.352
You will also learn how to describe what these things
do, how to give safe instructions for using them,

5
00:00:28.432 --> 00:00:31.924
and how to talk about working together as a crew.

6
00:00:32.004 --> 00:00:39.506
By the end of the unit, you will be ready to read
and enjoy this unit's mystery story, “The Attic Clue”,

7
00:00:39.586 --> 00:00:46.869
about a class in Rwanda who discover old tools in
a dusty attic and build something amazing together.

8
00:00:46.949 --> 00:00:52.993
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:53.073 --> 00:01:01.618
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
describe many tools, machines, and everyday items in English.

10
00:01:01.698 --> 00:01:08.893
You will also describe an object using adjectives
and a relative clause with who, that, or which.

11
00:01:08.973 --> 00:01:15.194
You will also say what people have to do
to stay safe when using tools and machines.

12
00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:17.969
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:18.049 --> 00:01:23.956
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
equipment, folder, briefcase, shield, stapler, hardware.

14
00:01:24.036 --> 00:01:28.710
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:32.408
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:32.488 --> 00:01:37.515
The reading sequence includes The Right
Tool for the Job and A Look at the Stars.

17
00:01:37.595 --> 00:01:38.398
Read actively.

18
00:01:38.478 --> 00:01:42.748
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:42.828 --> 00:01:46.847
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:46.927 --> 00:01:51.750
The first language focus is Defining
Relative Clauses (who, that, which).

21
00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:59.138
A defining relative clause is an extra part of a sentence
that tells us exactly which person or thing we mean.

22
00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:05.855
For example, in “the tool that joins papers,” the
words “that joins papers” tell us it is a stapler.

23
00:02:05.935 --> 00:02:10.355
This helps us describe the tools
and machines in this unit clearly.

24
00:02:10.435 --> 00:02:17.676
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:02:17.756 --> 00:02:21.939
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Describe an Everyday Item.

26
00:02:22.019 --> 00:02:26.079
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:26.159 --> 00:02:29.230
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:32.505
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:34.038
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:34.118 --> 00:02:40.638
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:40.718 --> 00:02:43.837
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:51.237
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
